{"agent_id":"driver","agent_seq":36,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T02:32:37.843890068Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c66a4338-cef5-44fa-bc52-a2230b30f5eb","comment_uuid":"2db6d53c-6832-4aa8-a04a-6298c63d9977","author":"driver","content":"ASES #192 fork fix complete on feature/ases-192-timeout-backstop (commit 0e014c45, issue #798). kickoff --timeout is now a non-destructive backstop (max(timeout*24, 24h), optional hook-config kickoff.timeout_backstop_secs override); watchdog rewritten as evidence recorder (terminal-sentinel exit per #138, writes .kickoff-stalled on stale heartbeat, never kills/nudges); kickoff status/list surface heartbeat age + stalled; worktree heartbeat hook ensured after init; .kickoff-stalled excluded from git. Tests: kickoff 190/190, full bin 2859/2859, lib 1783/1783, clippy clean for changed files, install OK. NOTE: pre-existing import.rs test-harness compile break on fork-local/agents fixed (2-line, mirrors #138 commit). Reviewer: verify 0e014c45; do NOT run live kickoff (orchestrator stages it).","created_at":"2026-08-06T02:32:37.837483383Z","kind":"handoff","signed_by":"SHA256:cx5PuRP0j7pktPKktl0WwbMp5uEwfFy9WoiBcgyhe18","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAguEQKo5PmNONBqYSfFi6Ry6tvLy9D5GLM9YcPkF7QNdoAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAVUuzE/eCg3MVuqtVgQgZnNDZ6z4zqD06FQffkQOC9D5HlgcQMNmsdYgQSJXB1RfqcbIkyH6VBT8mR23c3aHMAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:cx5PuRP0j7pktPKktl0WwbMp5uEwfFy9WoiBcgyhe18","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAguEQKo5PmNONBqYSfFi6Ry6tvLy9D5GLM9YcPkF7QNdoAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQE5mzaXb43W5/uPXSHAHorGRPLy3nop8QYAHzeng4z9sYYEftrbXEk+3bwVtupJ417caAkmG8gFJa7PsqjZFiAI="}
{"agent_id":"driver","agent_seq":37,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T03:07:31.258675868Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c66a4338-cef5-44fa-bc52-a2230b30f5eb","comment_uuid":"680cb85d-1291-4192-9b86-1d8a9140d82e","author":"driver","content":"test","created_at":"2026-08-06T03:07:31.251154112Z","kind":"verdict","signed_by":"SHA256:cx5PuRP0j7pktPKktl0WwbMp5uEwfFy9WoiBcgyhe18","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAguEQKo5PmNONBqYSfFi6Ry6tvLy9D5GLM9YcPkF7QNdoAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAVZNBU88QTjlTcLJJ/g/oxhtfg2Gx17lNIlAYTWatT2mGhR2yN50yCvz8JeUgcSE0k9cknbjHks+guL2Qy0GBAg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:cx5PuRP0j7pktPKktl0WwbMp5uEwfFy9WoiBcgyhe18","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAguEQKo5PmNONBqYSfFi6Ry6tvLy9D5GLM9YcPkF7QNdoAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQK55RIaJwzVfYASSvBRsfTGUTz8SWDKiLkJ7YyqJ5PbR/0mugq1oBcDnUX5qpUHMTJ4NeE2RGHHcygdEetICGAU="}
{"agent_id":"driver","agent_seq":38,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T03:08:31.930564949Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c66a4338-cef5-44fa-bc52-a2230b30f5eb","comment_uuid":"3e3f17de-e1ba-4f5c-8d05-9fb19fdff6df","author":"driver","content":"**Verdict**: CHANGES-REQUESTED\n\n**Summary**: The core ASES #192 contract is correctly implemented: --timeout is now a non-destructive backstop (max(timeout*24, 24h), hook-config overridable), threaded through every launch path including swarm and sentinel dispatch; the watchdog is a faithful port of #138 terminal-content exit with the nudge path fully removed and a correct stall-marker write. 190/190 kickoff tests pass, compilation is clean, and no new clippy issues are introduced. However, acceptance criterion (c) fails in the common case: ensure_worktree_heartbeat installs heartbeat.py without its mandatory sibling crosslink_config.py, so in a fresh worktree the hook crashes on import and the liveness-evidence stream (.crosslink/.cache/last-heartbeat) never flows — the watchdog then silently records nothing and status/list never surface the feature. Two smaller functional gaps (custom stall_marker not read by the monitor; docs still describing the removed nudge behavior) should also be addressed.\n\n**Findings**:\n1. MAJOR — crosslink/src/commands/kickoff/launch.rs:562-571 — ensure_worktree_heartbeat writes only heartbeat.py. heartbeat.py imports `from crosslink_config import find_crosslink_binary` at module top (resources/claude/hooks/heartbeat.py:17-19) BEFORE the mtime write (lines 52-70). In the exact scenario this function targets (fresh worktree where crosslink init short-circuits at init/mod.rs:869 because .crosslink/ and .claude/ are committed), .claude/hooks/crosslink_config.py is absent (.gitignore:65 ignores .claude/hooks/; git ls-tree confirms only work-check.py is tracked at repo root), so heartbeat.py raises ModuleNotFoundError on every PostToolUse, .crosslink/.cache/last-heartbeat is never touched, and the watchdog `if [ -f \"$HB\" ]` guard silently no-ops — no stall marker, no evidence, and kickoff status shows neither heartbeat age nor Stalled. Criterion (c) and the evidence side of (b) fail in the common case; the unit tests only assert file presence, not function. Evidence: static import/write ordering in heartbeat.py; init short-circuit at init/mod.rs:869; tracked-hook inventory via git ls-tree. Test test_ensure_worktree_heartbeat_writes_hook_when_missing (tests.rs:2861) does not execute the hook. Recommendation: also write CROSSLINK_CONFIG_PY (init/mod.rs:38, pub(crate)) alongside heartbeat.py (ideally the full managed hook set), or make heartbeat.py not depend on crosslink_config.\n\n2. MINOR — crosslink/src/commands/kickoff/monitor.rs:151,262 — readers hardcode .kickoff-stalled while the writer honors watchdog.stall_marker (launch.rs:150,169). A project configuring a custom stall_marker gets markers written to a path status/list never read, so the surfaced evidence silently disappears. Recommendation: have monitor paths read the config, or document stall_marker as write-only for now.\n\n3. MINOR — docs_src/reference/hook-config.qmd:188-220 — still documents the removed nudge behavior (sends a continue nudge, max_nudges before giving up, the surrounding --timeout will eventually clean up) and does not document watchdog.stall_marker or kickoff.timeout_backstop_secs. Doc drift introduced by this change.\n\n4. MINOR — crosslink/src/commands/kickoff/launch.rs:842-844 — docker path keeps --stop-timeout {timeout_secs} (the raw GUIDE value) with the now-misleading comment \"Hard-kill the container after the timeout (grace period = 10s on top)\". Docker --stop-timeout only sets the grace for a later user-invoked docker stop; it does not self-trigger, so this is not a #192 violation — but the comment misdescribes behavior and the guide value still flows into container config. Recommendation: pass backstop_secs and correct the comment. Also note container mode still has no watchdog (pre-existing, unchanged).\n\n5. NIT — crosslink/src/commands/kickoff/tests.rs:2770-2773 — !script.contains(\"[ -f {worktree}/.kickoff-status ]\") asserts against a literal {worktree} placeholder that can never appear in the generated script (format! substitutes it), so the assertion is vacuously true. The positive DONE*|FAILED*|CI_FAILED*|TIMEOUT* assertion already covers the #138 contract.\n\n6. NIT — crosslink/src/commands/kickoff/launch.rs:169,307 — stall_marker and the backstop value flow into the generated bash without escaping/validation. Consistent with the pre-existing interpolation pattern (worktree/session raw) and hook-config is trusted config, but a stall_marker containing a double-quote or shell metacharacters would break or escape the script. Consider validating or escaping.\n\n**Contract check**:\n(a) Backstop — PASS. timeout_backstop_secs = max(t*24, 86400) with saturating_mul (launch.rs:35-37); override threaded through launch_local (launch.rs:744), plan (plan.rs:248), and applied to the container inner wrapper (launch.rs:819,927,932); swarm (lifecycle.rs:739) and sentinel dispatch flow through kickoff::run -> launch_local, so they receive the backstop. No remaining kill-on-guide wrapper found.\n(b) Evidence watchdog — PASS at script level. #138 terminal-content exit ported verbatim (identical case patterns to 799ce67d); no send-keys/NUDGES anywhere in the generated script (verified in code and by negative test assertions); stall marker write is correct shell. Caveat: evidence flows only if the heartbeat file exists — which (c) fails to guarantee (Finding 1).\n(c) Worktree heartbeat — FAIL in the common case (Finding 1). HEARTBEAT_PY const exists (init/mod.rs:39, pub(crate), visible from kickoff::launch); settings.json PostToolUse matcher is present in the tracked template; the agent.json check is satisfied via agent::init in init_worktree_agent; but the missing crosslink_config.py dependency breaks the hook at runtime.\n(d) Monitor surfacing — PASS for the default marker: status prints Heartbeat age + Stalled (monitor.rs:136-162); discover_agents derives stalled only from running+marker (monitor.rs:258-267) and cannot mislabel done/failed/stopped (marker check requires final_status == running); normalize_status passes stalled through (helpers.rs:792-794); graph includes stalled (not in the skip list, graph.rs:77-83); default kickoff cleanup skips Stale-classed stalled agents (cleanup.rs:34-40) so there is no accidental kill; --status stalled filter works. Caveat: custom stall_marker not surfaced (Finding 2).\nBuild/tests — kickoff::tests 190/190 PASS (verified by running cargo test --bin crosslink kickoff::tests); full binary compiles (cargo test --bin crosslink --no-run clean); the claimed 2859/2859 full-suite count could not be reproduced here (the full suite hung past 25 min in this environment — appears infra-bound, not a compile failure); cargo clippy --bin crosslink -- -D warnings reports 24 errors, all pre-existing (the launch.rs:74 empty-line-after-doc-comment exists identically on fork-local/agents), none introduced by this change.\n\n**No-kill invariant**: Searched launch.rs, monitor.rs, cleanup.rs, plan.rs, run.rs, types.rs, helpers.rs, graph.rs, pipeline.rs, swarm/lifecycle.rs, swarm/status.rs, sentinel/dispatch.rs, container.rs for kill/send-keys/timeout wrappers. Remaining kill paths are all user-invoked: kickoff stop (monitor.rs:526-558), kickoff cleanup (cleanup.rs:194-238; default skips Stale), container stop/kill (container.rs:544-600). The only autonomous destroyer is the 24h+ backstop wrapper itself (intended) and the inert --stop-timeout config (Finding 4). is_timed_out (types.rs:395-410) is display-only (informational timed-out label in status/list); no code path kills on the guide value. No-kill invariant holds.","created_at":"2026-08-06T03:08:31.924209989Z","kind":"verdict","signed_by":"SHA256:cx5PuRP0j7pktPKktl0WwbMp5uEwfFy9WoiBcgyhe18","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAguEQKo5PmNONBqYSfFi6Ry6tvLy9D5GLM9YcPkF7QNdoAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAtvNDenSnBY+Yr0Q+PvaF0dobgRSA29stGjl7JX1agPVzrSbPwM0R1cNIbNYpVsZoceFsAbGjT7koWWnGBFYcDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:cx5PuRP0j7pktPKktl0WwbMp5uEwfFy9WoiBcgyhe18","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAguEQKo5PmNONBqYSfFi6Ry6tvLy9D5GLM9YcPkF7QNdoAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAfimn1TYz8pJq5Uy3cXLLkqV0NHUlJlKh07MR4YzG4I+TX+UCNYybdTuI+ZDmDQwpj5IBADh7b3b/QJGVqLFgc="}
